      "id": 118188,
      "name": "Rabit",
      "username": "Rabit",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-09-16T14:52:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I believe they've said they're going to just do oversized villain card sets, so the WotC villains and Wager Master will be available in a set GTG will release later with all those others that haven't been provided, yet.</p>\n<p>That was my understanding, anyway - could be wrong.</p>\n<p>Personally, I think this approach makes the most sense. There were problems with folks getting a couple here and there but not getting all of them, then the only way they could was to buy the later set, resulting in a lot of (perceived) wasted money / cards. This is a much cleaner, easier&nbsp;way of handling it - even if it means I don't get my oversized cards as soon as I want…  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/cry.png?v=9\" title=\":cry:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":cry:\"></p>\n<p><img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=9\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji only-emoji\" alt=\":wink:\"></p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:51:03.452Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
